* The average chain holds at most 0.75 pairs :: Right. The load factor is the average chain length.
* At least a quarter of the buckets are empty :: Right. There are at most 0.75 × size keys, so at most that many buckets can hold anything.
* `get` is O(1) on average :: Right. A short average chain means few comparisons.
- Every chain holds at most 1 pair :: The average is low, but some chains can still hold 2, 3 or more.
- No two keys are ever in the same bucket :: Collisions still happen; they're rarer, not impossible.
hint: The load factor is an average.
