right: The old chains are kept in `old`, new empty chains replace them, and every pair is appended at `key % new_size`. Old chain 0 split between new buckets 0 and 2.
wrong: Keep `old = self.buckets`, make `new_size` empty chains, then append every pair from every old chain to `self.buckets[key % new_size]`.
